# paper_restir: on-screen text in English (Project Fluent; lab/src/i18n.rs).

investigation-title = ReSTIR
investigation-summary = Bitterli et al. 2020: each pixel resamples light candidates in a tiny reservoir, then reuses its neighbours' and last frame's reservoirs, so many lights need only one shadow ray per pixel.
investigation-footer = Bitterli, Wyman, Pharr, Shirley, Lefohn, and Jarosz, ACM TOG 39(4), 2020, implemented from the paper. Every claim cites a section, a page, and an equation or algorithm line.
investigation-demo_hint = Drag to orbit; the dock's sliders set the method's parameters, what the scene shows, and the lights.
notice-credit = Implemented from the paper (MIT, the lab's own code).
scene-restir_room = The room with many lights
shot-room_title = ReSTIR in a room of many lights
shot-room = Room
controls-restir = ReSTIR
hints-restir = The paper's parameters: candidates, reuse in time and space, and how reservoirs are combined.
controls-view_group = View
hints-view = What the scene shows: the lit image, or the reservoirs after one stage.
controls-lights = Lights
hints-lights = The room's lights: how many, where along their paths, and how bright.
controls-candidates = Candidates (M)
help-restirCandidates = M, the candidates each pixel draws from the lights by power before choosing one (Alg. 3; 32 in the paper's results).
controls-temporal = Temporal reuse
help-restirTemporal = Combine each pixel's reservoir with last frame's at the same point (Alg. 5, lines 11-14).
controls-spatial_passes = Spatial rounds (n)
help-restirSpatialPasses = n, the rounds in which each pixel combines its neighbours' reservoirs (2 for the paper's biased results, 1 unbiased).
controls-neighbours = Neighbours (k)
help-restirNeighbours = k, the neighbours each round combines (5 biased, 3 unbiased in the paper).
controls-radius = Neighbour radius
help-restirRadius = The radius, in pixels, the neighbours are drawn in (30 in the paper).
controls-visibility_reuse = Visibility reuse
help-restirVisibilityReuse = Test each pixel's chosen sample with a shadow ray before reuse, and drop it if it is occluded.
controls-unbiased = Unbiased combination
help-restirUnbiased = Combine reservoirs with the unbiased weight of Alg. 6 (count only the sources that could have produced the sample) instead of Alg. 4's.
controls-geometry_test = Geometry test
help-restirGeometryTest = Skip a neighbour whose camera distance differs by more than 10% or whose normal turns more than 25 degrees.
controls-temporal_clamp = Temporal clamp
help-restirTemporalClamp = Last frame's M is at most this many times this frame's (20 in the paper).
controls-view = View mode
help-restirView = 0 the lit image; 1 the light each pixel's sample is on; 2 M; 3 W; 4 whether the sample is visible.
controls-accumulate = Accumulate
help-restirAccumulate = Average the frames while nothing moves, converging to a reference.
controls-stage = Stage shown
help-restirStage = Which reservoirs are shaded: 0 after RIS, 1 after visibility, 2 after temporal reuse, 3 after spatial reuse.
controls-light_count = Lights on
help-lightCount = How many of the room's 64 lights are on.
controls-light_phase = Light motion
help-lightPhase = Where the lights are along their paths, 0 to 1.
controls-light_intensity = Light intensity
help-lightIntensity = A scale on every light's radiance.
pass-restirPrepassFS = The pre-pass: each pixel's depth, normal, object, albedo, and roughness.
pass-restirForwardFS = The scene pass: the shaded samples on the surfaces, the lights drawn with their radiance.
pass-restirCandidates = Streaming RIS (Alg. 3): M candidates per pixel, from the lights by power, streamed through one reservoir.
pass-restirVisibility = Visibility reuse: a shadow ray to each pixel's selected sample; W set to 0 where it is occluded.
pass-restirTemporal = Temporal reuse: each reservoir combined with last frame's at the same point.
pass-restirSpatial = Spatial reuse: each reservoir combined with k neighbours' within the radius.
pass-restirKeep = The frame's reservoirs, and their surfaces, kept for the next frame.
pass-restirShade = Shading: the sample's contribution times W, with its visibility; and the running mean.
listing-frame-title = ReSTIR in one frame (Alg. 5)
listing-frame-dispatch = once per frame, for every pixel
controls-pick = P
hints-pick = The pixel P the demonstration follows (click the scene to pick another), and how far its candidates are streamed.
controls-pick_u = P across
help-pickU = P's place across the viewport, 0 at the left edge, 1 at the right.
controls-pick_v = P down
help-pickV = P's place down the viewport, 0 at the top, 1 at the bottom.
controls-ris_step = Candidates streamed
help-risStep = How many of P's candidates have been fed to its reservoir so far, from none to M.
controls-spatial_step = Neighbours combined
help-spatialStep = How many of P's neighbours its first round has combined so far, in order, P's own reservoir first; 16 is all.
controls-ris_weigh = Lines by weight
help-risWeigh = 0 draws every candidate's line alike; 1 draws each as bright as its weight, its target over its probability.
controls-ris_pick = Pick marker
help-risPick = A marker running along the streamed candidates laid end to end by weight: each is lit for its share of the weight sum. 0 is off; 1 shows the kept one.
controls-seed = Seed
help-restirSeed = The seed of the frame's random numbers; below 0, a new one every frame. A fixed seed draws the same candidates each frame.
